WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.836
-President Biden
is back from his summit

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.404
with Russian president
Vladimir Putin,

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:07.173
and now the very same people
who approved of

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.975
Donald Trump's
friendly attitude toward Putin

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.676
are claiming Biden
wasn't tough enough.

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.779
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:16.816
♪♪

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.318
President Biden has returned
from his first overseas trip,

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:21.788
which, once again, showed the
stark contrast between

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.756
his presidency
and that of Trump.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.326
Even Putin himself
was willing to acknowledge

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.594
the difference
in this exchange with reporters.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:31.764
-The conversation
was quite constructive.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:37.303
And I once again understood
that President Biden

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.105
is an experienced statesman.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.340
He is very different
from President Trump.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.110
-I mean, to be fair,
everybody is.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.679
Putin's like a kid describing
his mom's new boyfriend.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.782
"Yeah, she dumped Sammy 'cause
he got fired from Guitar Center

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:52.252
for eating Slim Jims on the job
and spending all day

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.786
playing the solo from
'In the Air Tonight'

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.955
on the drum kit,
and now she's out with Keith.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.857
He's a dentist
who collects stamps.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:01.093
He's very different.
The other day, we had salad!"

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:02.795
It's weird to hear that
description come from Putin

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.063
of all people.

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.732
Although, I bet his
relationship with Trump was

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.734
less like buddy-buddy
and more like

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.935
former KGB agent
and useful moron.

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:12.872
Like, Putin obviously
preferred Trump policy-wise,

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.241
but there's got to be
a small part of him

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.178
that's relieved not to have
to make small talk with Trump

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.213
anymore in those long
one-on-one meetings.

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:22.715
I mean, Trump
is like your weed dealer

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.084
who drops off a baggie and
then won't leave.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:27.720
"I'm just gonna roll one up
before I get an Uber.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.890
So, anyway, Vlad, it's 1986,
and I'm at Studio 54

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.192
with Tommy Lee
and Wally Backman.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.461
Bad guy, nasty guy.
Nice to me, though.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.130
He was in a platoon
with Tim Teufel.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.598
Do you remember Tim Teufel?"

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.266
"I do not know this Teufel man."

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.901
"Well, the 'Late Night'
crew remembers him,

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.569
I promise you that.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:44.737
I promise you that.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:48.507
You can bend John O'Malley's ear
about Tim Teufel.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:49.909
He'd be happy to fill you in."

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.378
So, even Putin
was willing to admit that

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.748
he was dealing with a more
experienced statesman, in Biden.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.750
Our key allies in
the G7 and NATO

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.985
also seemed excited
throughout Biden's trip

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:02.255
about the fact that they were
finally dealing with

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:05.090
a U.S. president interested in
global cooperation

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.192
to solve common problems.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.894
And, yet --
this will shock you --

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.830
Fox News had
a very different takeaway.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.765 line:0%
-Unfortunately,
we've seen a lot of weakness

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.968 line:0%
from President Biden
as it relates to Russia.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.470 line:0%
-Vladimir received
a massive platform

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.573 line:0%
in exchange for
zero concessions whatsoever.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.742 line:0%
And Putin then
used that platform

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:26.379 line:0%
to take shot after shot after
shot at our country,

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.213 line:0%
the United States of America.

00:02:28.213 --> 00:02:32.552 line:0%
Joe, of course, was nowhere to
be found correcting the record,

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:35.455 line:0%
because he was afraid
to stand next to Vladimir,

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.957 line:0%
probably because he
is not capable of doing it.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:41.360 line:0%
-It makes us look ridiculous.
It is embarrassing.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.795 line:0%
-I thought The Washington Post
had a great line, too.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.498 line:0%
It said -- And I don't even know
if they were being --

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.934 line:0%
they knew they were
being funny, I think.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.603 line:0%
They say, "Joe Biden's
pessimistic approach

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.805 line:0%
to the summit
seems to have paid off."

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.039 line:0%
Fantastic!

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:56.742 line:0%
So I had low expectations
and I hit all my goals.

00:02:56.742 --> 00:03:00.146 line:0%
-Thank God the two of them
didn't stand next each other.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:03.316 line:0%
You know, Joe Biden is
a kindly old man,

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:06.252 line:0%
and he looked tired
and he didn't have vigor.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.555 line:0%
Compare that to Putin,
who is a killer,

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:11.357 line:0%
who does have
the wind at his back.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.825
-Okay, I compared them.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.361
Am I supposed to be on
Team Killer?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.495
I mean, that sounded
like something

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.631
Samantha would say
when comparing lovers.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.400
"I don't have time
for kindly old men.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.702
I need a killer
with the wind at his back.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:26.505
And my back!"

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:29.442
Also, this idea that, somehow,
Biden comes off as tired

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.577
just because he doesn't use
his press conferences

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:34.813
to rant and rave for hours about
insane [bleep] is so stupid.

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:37.182
I mean, Trump is the one
who constantly looked exhausted

00:03:37.182 --> 00:03:39.485
and drained of energy,
because he spent all his time

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.553
screaming at reporters
and pulling all-nighters

00:03:41.553 --> 00:03:42.588
to hate-watch cable news.

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:43.623
I mean, look at him.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.091
He looks like an old umpire

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.627
at the end of a July
Little League doubleheader,

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.462
and you guys
are complaining that Biden

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.063
didn't do a joint
press conference

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:52.398
with Putin to correct him?

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.867
Trump did a joint
press conference with Putin,

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.402
and all he did
was agree with him.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.170
When those two did
a press conference together,

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.506
Trump was basically Putin's
Ed McMahon.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.508
"Russia had nothing to do
with election hacking,

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:06.279
and anyone who disagrees will be
sent to the Slauson Cut-Off,

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.914
where we will
cut off their Slauson."

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.083
[ Laughs ] "Very good!"

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:14.019
Now, Biden's summit with Putin
was a tricky balancing act.

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:16.089
On the one hand, you want to
hold Putin accountable

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.790
for his actions,
but on the other,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.925
you don't want it to
escalate into conflict,

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:21.160
as Biden explained.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.029
-When you run a country
that does not abide by

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:26.366
international norms,
and, yet, you need those

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:29.935
international norms
to be somehow managed

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:31.971
so that you can participate
in the benefits

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.140
that flow from them,
it hurts you.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.843
That's not a satisfying answer.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.011
"Biden said he'd invade Russia."

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:40.346
You know, it is not --
You know...

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.482
By the way, that was a joke.

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.715
That's not true.

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:46.852
-Thanks for clarifying,
but, also, no more jokes.

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:48.320
Especially after
meeting with Putin.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.357
That's the last place we need
you to workshop new material.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.527
But I understand and appreciate
the point Biden was making.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.928
Diplomacy can be complicated.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.696
We can hold Putin accountable
for his actions

00:04:57.696 --> 00:05:00.632
and avoid conflict with Russia,
which no one wants.

00:05:00.632 --> 00:05:03.502
I mean, I don't know if 30 Rock
even has a bomb shelter,

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.471
but if it does, I don't want to
get stuck down there

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:08.708
with Wally, the two of us eating
canned beans in our underwear

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.777
for the rest of our lives,
while he holds up cue cards,

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.712
asking me if I want to
play Scrabble.

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:15.181
And then, when we run out of
food, we open the hatch,

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.949
only to find out it had
been a false alarm.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.118
And bad news -- we've
been underground for 17 years.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.786
But good news --
we're back just in time for

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:22.154
the Broadway revival
of my musical,

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.623
"Cicada, Cicada,"
with it's original cast --

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:26.526
Baranski, Fierstein, Lane,

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.961
and Jason Sudeikis
in the role of Jason Cicadas.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.130
And for those of you wondering
what role that is,

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.498
I'd describe it as kind of
like -- I don't know --

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.034
the stage manager in
"Our Town."

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.936
He kind of just walks you
through the action.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:41.173
His first line is,
"Oh, I didn't see you there."

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:44.610
The point is,
we can hold Putin accountable

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.146
for election interference
and human-rights abuses

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:49.182
while also avoiding
a tense confrontation

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.516
with a nuclear-armed power,

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.118
and Biden did his best
to walk a fine line.

00:05:53.118 --> 00:05:54.754
That doesn't mean
he didn't make mistakes.

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.322
For example,
while he was talking about

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.256
Russian election interference,
he said this.

00:05:58.256 --> 00:06:00.258
-How would it be if the
United States were viewed by

00:06:00.258 --> 00:06:03.662
the rest of the world as
interfering with the elections,

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:07.099
directly, of other countries
and everybody knew it?

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:08.701
-How would it be? Hold on.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.003
Let me consult this thing
I found the other day.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.838
It's called a book.

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:13.940
And let me see.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.242
And oh, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:18.344
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:21.747
Oh, Joe, you do not want
to read this.

00:06:21.747 --> 00:06:24.216
I mean, seriously, dude,
you can condemn Putin

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.485
for interfering in our elections
and colluding with Trump

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:29.688
to subvert our democracy without
ignoring our own history.

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:32.458
I mean, one study found that
the U.S. has intervened

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:35.360
in foreign elections more than
80 times, worldwide,

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.363
between 1946 and 2000.

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:38.731
80 times!

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.466
The U.S. has intervened
in foreign elections

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:41.734
almost as many times as

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.970
we've played that
stupid Vanilla Ice clip.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.705
-Uh, like, it goes, "Ding, ding,
ding, ding-a-ding, ding.

00:06:46.705 --> 00:06:48.341
Ding, ding, ding,
ding-a-ding, ding."

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:49.609
That's the way theirs goes.

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.577
Ours goes, "Ding, ding, ding,
ding-a-ding, ding.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.512
Tshh, ding, ding, ding,
ding-a-ding, ding."

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:54.714
That little, bitty ting.

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:55.748
It's not the same.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:56.782
-We had to do it.

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:58.484
If we do it three times,
we get a free sub

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:01.053
made by Vanilla Ice.

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:03.155
And, by the way, we've heard
feedback from some of you guys

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:04.356
that we went to
the well too many times on

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:05.591
the Vanilla Ice clip,

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:07.427
while others seem to be
enjoying it a great deal.

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:09.629
So, we want to know
what you think.

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:11.964 line:0%
Please go to @seacaptainpolls
and vote for

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:16.235 line:0%
"stop," "collaborate,"
or "listen."

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:17.870 line:0%
The point is,
both things can be true.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.539
We can be honest about
our own past

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:21.440
while also standing up
to election interference

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.042
and human-rights abuses by
brutal autocrats like Putin.

00:07:24.042 --> 00:07:25.944
In fact,
learning from our own past

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:28.113
and striving to be better
is a good thing.

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:30.182
Trump and his cronies are the
ones who have been cozying up

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:32.351
to dictators, working to
subvert our democracy,

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.786
and actively trying to
whitewash our own history

00:07:34.786 --> 00:07:36.956
by censoring teachers or
rewriting textbooks.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:39.558
The GOP has taken
a hard turn against democracy,

00:07:39.558 --> 00:07:41.260
and two polls published
this week have found that

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.696
Putin has a better
net favorable rating

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:46.598
among Republicans than Biden
does, which is insane.

00:07:46.598 --> 00:07:48.167
Trump himself
never seemed happier

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.568
than when he was
meeting with dictators.

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:51.070
He always had that rictus grin

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.039
like the clown at the end
of the mini-golf course.

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:56.341
It's all a part of the GOP's
growing contempt for democracy

00:07:56.341 --> 00:07:58.744
and their open attempts
to subvert our elections.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:00.680
And now another
new poll found that

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:03.148
more than half of
GOP voters actually believe

00:08:03.148 --> 00:08:05.384
the big lie that
Republicans keep spreading

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:06.885
about the 2020 election.

00:08:06.885 --> 00:08:09.488
-A new poll out today
says that more than half --

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:11.156
more than half --
of Republican voters

00:08:11.156 --> 00:08:14.427
think election reviews
will change the 2020 outcome.

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:16.428
-I mean, it's been seven months,
and they still think

00:08:16.428 --> 00:08:17.963
Trump's going to come back
because they trust

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:20.632
a pillow magnate more than
the sanctity of our elections.

00:08:20.632 --> 00:08:23.069
At some point, you just
have to accept an outcome

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:24.336
that you don't agree with
and say,

00:08:24.336 --> 00:08:27.573
"It's Bran, and we can't do
anything about it."

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:28.774
Sidenote,
speaking of elections --

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:30.709
I voted early for
New York mayor yesterday

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:33.512
and I was incredibly impressed
by how seriously they took it.

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:35.481
For example, when they
asked for my signature,

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.016
I just scribbled it
the way you'd sign

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.016
a credit-card receipt,
and they said,

00:08:38.016 --> 00:08:39.051
"This isn't a match."

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:41.019
And I said,
"Do you know who I am?

00:08:41.019 --> 00:08:42.588
I wrote 'Cicada, Cicada.'"

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:44.357
And they said, "Prove it."
And I said...

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.691
♪ 17 years with my head
in the mud ♪

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:46.925
♪ And my heart in my throat ♪

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:48.961
♪ And my wings that
are yearning to fly ♪

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.930
And then they kicked me out.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.765
And I said, "Your loss,

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:55.434
'cause I was voting for
de Blasio again."

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.536
The point is,
if the GOP gets the chance

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.138
to overturn an election
in the future,

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:00.439
they could very well do it.

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:02.942
I mean, what if they
win back the House in 2022

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.976
and then Biden
wins re-election in 2024?

00:09:04.976 --> 00:09:07.346
Do you really think Republicans

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:09.081
will suddenly regain
their sanity?

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:11.249
I mean, I was trapped in a room
with a sea-captain painting

00:09:11.249 --> 00:09:13.419
for a few months, and when I
returned to the studio,

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:16.288
it's not like
I immediately became sane again.

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:18.023
I mean, sure, I didn't bring
the painting with me,

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:19.758
but I talk to Wally
all the time,

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:22.294
and now he's so famous
that he just got asked to do

00:09:22.294 --> 00:09:23.929
a "Carpool Karaoke."

00:09:23.929 --> 00:09:26.098
-♪ Fresh new kicks ♪
♪ And pants ♪

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:28.634
♪ You gotta like that ♪
♪ Now you know you wanna dance ♪

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:29.634
-They're gonna
let you do that song?

00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:30.669
-Oh, yeah.

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:31.670
They said they could
afford to play it

